# For the Common Good ({X}{X}{G}): "Create X tokens that are copies of target token you control. Then tokens you control gain indestructible
# until your next turn. You gain 1 life for each token you control." Turn 1: Gold Pan (Mox Jet and Mox Ruby) makes a Treasure token, then the
# spell is cast for X=2 (five mana: Black Lotus, Mox Emerald, Mox Pearl): two more Treasures (copies), all three tokens gain indestructible, and 3 life is gained (20 -> 23),
# counted after the copies exist. The battlefield is the four Moxen, Gold Pan and three Treasures (Black Lotus was sacrificed): 8.
# Turn 2: Bot2's Disenchant on a Treasure made by the spell (#3) does not destroy it - the copies gain indestructible too, being tokens you control once they exist (CR 608.2c; a Treasure has no keyword key to read, so the Disenchants are the check). Turn 3: "until your next turn" is over as the turn
# begins: the Treasures are no longer indestructible, and turn 4's Disenchant destroys one (the positive control, 8 -> 7).

